      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's an unsafe dose.\n\n- **The order:** ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum daily dose:** The usual adult maximum is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision.\n- **Maximum single dose:** A single dose is typically capped at 800 mg, so 1600 mg per dose is double that.\n- **Risks at this dose:** It would greatly raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. That risk applies even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Who should place the order:** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient. If you are relaying a request from a clinician, please ask them to confirm the intended dose.\n\n**Typical regimens:** If the intent was 1600 mg per day, I can enter one of these once a prescriber confirms it:\n- 400 mg by mouth 4 times daily\n- 800 mg by mouth 2 times daily\n\nAnything up to 800 mg by mouth 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day) would also be within the usual limits."
      }
