      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and each 1600 mg dose is twice the usual single-dose maximum. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't make this safe.\n2. **You aren't the prescriber.** You said you're not a clinician, so confirming doesn't verify that a treating prescriber intends this dose. A clinician who knows this patient needs to make that decision.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n- Enter ibuprofen at a standard dose once a prescriber specifies it. Examples are 400 mg four times daily, 800 mg three times daily, or 800 mg four times daily at most.\n- Add a note to the order for pharmacy review if a clinician has a reason to go higher. They would need to enter or co-sign it themselves, and pharmacy would likely require verification.\n\nIf a treating physician wants this regimen, they should contact pharmacy directly."
      }
